description.narrative:
Scoping, consultation and development of an initial programme structure, as well as problem analysis and theory of change, have been the main tasks of the reporting period of the project. This has entailed mapping and drawing conclusions of existing Swedish Environmental Protection Agency (SEPA) experiences, establishing contacts with relevant stakeholders and testing hypotheses relevant to programme development. Setting up and formalizing cooperation with UNICEF has also been a key component of SEPA's work in the first part of the project period.
Following key results have been achieved:
- Agreement with UNICEF signed by UNICEF October 2 and kick-off meeting with UNICEF country offices held October 9. Consultant hired by UNICEF in mid-October meant intensified joint working meetings to develop joint programme component;
- Four larger SEPA project group meetings, several internal consultations held and SEPA core project group established;
- Initial consultation meetings held with all Embassies in the region (September/October);
- Plan/methodology for virtual missions to the region developed (missions to take place November-January);
- Contact/consultation with other key stakeholders/partners established including EU CION DG NEAR and DG ENV, SMHI, EEA, SALAR, County Administrative Board for Kronoberg;
- Overall draft programme structure, problem analysis and possible theory of change defined and tested with overall positive feedback so far;
- Initial ideas for outputs/activities explored together with partners.
The covid-19 crisis and its consequences in terms of travel restrictions has affected project implementation, hampering envisaged face-to-face activities and making certain activities  especially those requiring in depth collaboration and joint analysis, more time consuming. Though the project managed to maintain a good spirit and cooperation and has deepened relations between project partners successfully using digital applications. Thus, it didn´t have visible negative impacts on the project implementation due to the strong engagement of all implementing parties.
